🗂️ Job Search Dossier — AI-Powered Career Toolkit
An interactive, terminal/VS Code-inspired single-page web app that packages a complete personal job search and branding toolkit — built as part of my Claude AI Challenge.
🔗 Live Demo / File: Urooba_Job_Dossier.html
👩‍💻 Built by: Urooba Zahir
💡 What It Does
This dossier is a personal career command center — a scrollable, dark-themed "developer file" containing 12 ready-to-use sections for job hunting, generated entirely from my resume, portfolio, and LinkedIn profile:
ATS-Friendly Cover Letter
Recruiter Outreach Email
Hiring Manager Email
LinkedIn Connection Requests
Referral Request Message
Follow-Up Email
30-Second Professional Introduction
Top 10 Job Titles Matched to My Profile
Key Strengths Recruiters Will Notice
Skill Gap Analysis + Learning Roadmap
Personal Brand Summary & Recruiter Headline
Interview Talking Points (STAR-format ready)
Every section comes with a one-tap copy button — so the content can be used immediately for real applications, no editing required.
✨ Features
🖥️ Terminal-style header with macOS traffic-light dots and a typed command-line animation
📌 Sticky, auto-highlighting navigation bar — tracks scroll position and highlights the active section in real time
📋 Copy-to-clipboard on every section card
🎨 Custom dark theme using JetBrains Mono + Inter typography
📱 Fully responsive — built mobile-first
🛠️ Built With
HTML5
CSS3 (custom properties, responsive design, IntersectionObserver-driven UI)
Vanilla JavaScript (no frameworks/dependencies)
🎯 Why I Built This
Job hunting as a student juggling two internships meant I needed every outreach message, cover letter, and talking point ready before I needed it — not written from scratch under pressure. This project turns that prep work into a single, shareable, visually engaging artifact.
🙌 Part of the Claude AI Challenge
Built as part of a structured daily AI-build challenge — turning real personal/professional needs into polished, deployable single-file web apps.
